WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.650
Our next guest has truly set the gold standard.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.330
She is an incredible, innovative art teacher

3
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.410
from Arizona, and she re-engaged her students

4
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.620
in the pandemic by bringing the outside world

5
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.570
of art and nature straight to her students' screens.

6
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.670
In the last year she's taken her 400 students

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.520
on over 40 virtual field trips.

8
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.880
Now this is a person I want to have this discussion with.

9
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.446
Please welcome the amazing teacher, Candace Greene.

10
00:00:27.446 --> 00:00:28.480
Hi, Candace!
(audience clapping)

11
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.060
Hello, hi, thank you for having me. I'm so excited.

12
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.610
Well, can I ask what gave you the idea to do this?

13
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.480
Because I was reading that, you know,

14
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.830
kind of like 40% of your students

15
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.790
at one point were attending.

16
00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.590
They probably felt disengaged, you know,

17
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.160
the pandemic was starting.

18
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.203
Everybody was freaking out.

19
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.320
What gave you the idea to do this?

20
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.050
Because now you have complete engagement with your students.

21
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.490 line:15%
Yes, so, you know, in the first quarter

22
00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.690 line:15%
of the school year, it was really difficult.

23
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.870 line:15%
I have over 400 students and only about 40% of my students

24
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.180 line:15%
were showing up on a regular basis to our in,

25
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.840 line:15%
to the virtual classroom.

26
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.900 line:15%
And the ones that did show up,

27
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.430 line:15%
they were not turning their cameras on.

28
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.040 line:15%
They wouldn't unmute and talk.

29
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.080
They wouldn't even type in the chat.

30
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.150
So I would just be talking to myself for 45 minutes.

31
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.370
And then they weren't turning in assignments.

32
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:27.760
And in the regular classroom every year

33
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.460
my favorite thing to do is to go on field trips,

34
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.630
I love field trips.

35
00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.920
I love exposing my kids to the arts around them.

36
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.540
And I write many grants every year.

37
00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.360
And I just thought, wow, what about this opportunity

38
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.360
that I have...

39
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.540
It's easier to do field trips this way

40
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.970
and still expose my students and hopefully will engage them

41
00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.260
and make them want to come into the virtual classroom.

42
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.270
So I started these live virtual field trips.

43
00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.338
I love that.
(audience applauding)

44
00:01:56.338 --> 00:01:57.660
I mean, just think about

45
00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.520
that's the innovation were talking about

46
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.380
where, you know, we could have been so limited

47
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.370 line:15%
with what we've been through,

48
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.070 line:15%
but you've taken this technology

49
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.010 line:15%
and really just changed the game.

50
00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.330 line:15%
You've taken over 40 trips, traveled hundreds of miles.

51
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.510
I know you get results.

52
00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:15.080
The kids are totally engaged, right?

53
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.070
Oh, absolutely.

54
00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:21.350
My numbers now, I went from 40% of students to showing up

55
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.574
to 99% of my students-

56
00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:25.877
(Drew gasping)
Amazing!

57
00:02:25.877 --> 00:02:28.850
Right? That's phenomenal.

58
00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.280
You put together art kits to engage your students

59
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.250
in like a more hands-on kind of way.

60
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.410
Can you tell us about those?

61
00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:39.600
Sure, I knew that while we were at home,

62
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.700
these students wouldn't have access to art supplies

63
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.980
like they would have if we were in the classroom.

64
00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.220 line:15%
So I wanted to be able to give each of my students supplies.

65
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:55.070 line:15%
So I started like asking for donations on Facebook

66
00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:00.070
and gathering supplies, and I wanted to give each kid a kit.

67
00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.610
So right now I'm at 380 kits and my goal is 400,

68
00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.580
so all my students will be able to get art supplies.

69
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.410
So I've got 20 more to go.

70
00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.040
Well, your generosity of time, spirit, and energy

71
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.970
has certainly made a huge difference

72
00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.230
in the lives of these students.

73
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.430
And our friends at OOLY want to help you finish those kits.

74
00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.176
So they're gonna send you $9,000 worth of art supplies!

75
00:03:25.176 --> 00:03:27.718
(audience cheering)

76
00:03:27.718 --> 00:03:30.968
Craft paint, colored pencils, and more!

77
00:03:31.859 --> 00:03:35.380
Thank you so much.
Thank you.

78
00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.130
Candace, $9,000.

79
00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.590
You inspired this company to do that.

80
00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.110
That's amazing. Thank you so much.

81
00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.970
Oh my gosh.

82
00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:50.970
I am so grateful for what you do, because I do think

83
00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.670
that getting people interested in the arts

84
00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.670
is not sort of the easiest thing to do sometimes.

85
00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:04.670
And the fact that you decided to see 40% interest

86
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.320
in online, virtual learning.

87
00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.160
I'm a parent. I saw my kids too.

88
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.330
They couldn't get engaged. They were struggling.

89
00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.880
And I was struggling as a parent.

90
00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.830
And so for you to see this discrepancy

91
00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:26.430
and try to make it interesting, to try and rope them back in

92
00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:30.070
and harness them and get them re-ignited,

93
00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.880
that's what you did, Candace.

94
00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.110
It's amazing.
It is.

95
00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.990
Thank you.
Thank you.

96
00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.780
Thank you for what you do and thank you to OOLY.

97
00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.140
Hey!
(screams) Love you,

98
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.473
OOLY, I love you, thank you!

99
00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.440
Amazing, I just think about,

100
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.200
in a time when we were literally locked down,

101
00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.460
you just showed your kids the world.

102
00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.610
And I think that is amazing what you did, Candace.

103
00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.600
Ross, that was perfectly put.

104
00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.064
Well, she did it.

105
00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.810
Thank you.
(audience cheering)

106
00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:00.643
Thank you, Candace.

107
00:05:00.643 --> 00:05:02.810
And I really hope that what you did

108
00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.700
continues to inspire other people.

109
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.530
May we keep expanding each other's horizons.

110
00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.680 line:15%
When you think you're limited, Ross is right,

111
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.673 line:15%
you showed the possibilities.

112
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:17.910 line:15%
Thank you.
Thank you,

113
00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.076
Candace Greene.

114
00:05:19.076 --> 00:05:21.743 line:15%
(upbeat music)

